[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :actor/wave 3, :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-plating-decision :finalize-plating-operation :authorize-plating-run :proceed-with-plating-run :finalize-chemical-safety-clearance :declare-batch-safe-for-handling :declare-plated-batch-safe-for-handling :declare-batch-safe-for-shipment :clear-batch-for-shipment :override-plant-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799007535-cloud-itonami-isco-7535-pelt-dressers-tanners-fellmongers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the plating run" "proceed with the electroplating run" "authorize the plating run" "authorize the electroplating run" "finalize the plating decision" "finalize the plating operation" "declare the batch safe for handling" "declare the plated batch safe for handling" "declare the batch safe for shipment" "declare the plated batch safe for shipment" "clear the batch for shipment" "clear the plated batch for handling" "finalize the chemical safety clearance" "finalize the chemical-safety clearance" "declare the chemical bath safety cleared" "declare the plating bath safety cleared" "override the plant safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override plant safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799008122, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-work-record :flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation}}}", :actor/domain :manufacturing/metal-finishing-plating-coating-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:no-plater :no-facility :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-action], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "8122", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799008122: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8122 Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Machine Operators plant scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8122\n-- Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Machine Operators** only. This\nis Wave3 (production/trades); Wave0/1/2 are 100% complete and the\nentire 75xx craft-trades range is complete; this actor begins the\n81xx/82xx plant-and-machine-operator range (`kotoba.occupation.wave/\nwave-of \"8122\"` resolves to wave 3).\n\n`gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122` returned a clean\n404 before any work began -- this was a genuinely fresh scaffold, not a\nresume of prior partial work.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8122\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8122\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath, and cross-checked with `pr-str` to rule out a false read from\n`println`'s unquoted string rendering), and its `:name` read exactly\n\"Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Machine Operators\" -- confirming\nthe premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was\n`:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-\nledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`. This ADR and its companion\nregistry edit promote the `8122` entry to `:implemented`.\n\n**Electroplating chemical hazard dimension.** Metal Finishing, Plating\nand Coating Machine Operators run electroplating lines using chemical\nbaths (historically including cyanide-based and chromium-based\nsolutions) -- a real chemical-exposure hazard, alongside electrical\nhazard from electroplating current. This actor does NOT model direct\nplating-equipment operation authority or chemical-safety-clearance\nauthority. It is deliberately restricted to PLANT SCHEDULING and\nLOGISTICS COORDINATION around the occupation (production-run/\ninventory/progress-record logging, crew/shift scheduling, safety-\nconcern escalation, and plating-chemicals/raw-material procurement\ncoordination) -- never the plating-operation-execution decision or the\nchemical-safety-clearance decision itself, and never an override of a\nplant safety officer's judgment. The closed proposal-op allowlist\nstructurally excludes any op that could directly finalize such a\ndecision, and the governor independently, permanently hard-blocks any\nproposal whose rationale text names such a finalization action,\nregardless of the declared `:op` or confidence -- this is not an\nescalation path a human can approve through, it is an outright,\nstructural refusal at every maturity level.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7535`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7535)\n(Pelt Dressers, Tanners and Fellmongers -- a closely related chemical-\nprocessing hazard pattern: tanning chemicals historically including\nchromium compounds), independently re-cloned and read in full this\nsession. Its `tannerycoord.{store,advisor,governor,actor}` module\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph shape, closed op-allowlist and\nscope-exclusion self-trip-guard design translate almost 1:1 onto this\noccupation's own chemical-hazard-adjacent coordination scope, so this\nADR's `platingcoord.*` modules follow the same shape with domain terms\nsubstituted (tanner -> plater, tannery -> plating facility/plant, shop\nsafety officer -> plant safety officer, tanning-execution -> plating-\noperation-execution).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for metal finishing,\nplating and coating machine operators, following the SAME\ngoverned-actor architecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*`\nactor in this fleet: **Plating Plant Scheduling Coordination Advisor\n⊣ PlatingCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family),\nwith an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **plant scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never plating-equipment operation authority** -- it must NEVER\nbe designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\nplating-operation-execution decision or a chemical-safety-clearance\ndecision.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n  logging only\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n  only\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a chemical-exposure/ventilation/\n  electrical-hazard/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates\n  immediately, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- plating-chemicals/raw-material\n  procurement proposal only\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles a plating-operation-execution finalization decision or a\nchemical-safety-clearance finalization decision -- these are\nstructurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely, not merely gated\nbehind escalation.\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Plater unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered plater (crew member) record\n   (`:no-plater`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   plater is.\n2. **Facility unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered plating facility/line record\n   (`:no-facility`).\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`; the governor never dispatches hardware\n   itself and never operates plating equipment itself).\n4. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n5. **Scope-excluded action** -- the proposal's `:op` or `:rationale`\n   must never name a plating-operation-execution finalization, a\n   chemical-safety-clearance finalization, or a plant-safety-officer-\n   judgment override (`:scope-excluded-action`), REGARDLESS of the\n   declared `:op` or confidence. This is a hard, PERMANENT block --\n   there is no maturity level or confidence at which this actor may\n   auto-commit or human-approve its way past this rule; it is an\n   outright refusal, not an escalation.\n\n### Escalation gates (always human sign-off)\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's always-escalate path). The only channel by\n  which the robot may surface a chemical-exposure/ventilation/\n  electrical-hazard/equipment-condition observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000) -- always needs human sign-off,\n  independent of confidence (boundary verified as exclusive by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`: exactly-at-threshold\n  commits, over-threshold escalates).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, CLAUDE.md)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare NOUNS (e.g.\n\"cyanide\", \"chromium\", \"electroplating\") can accidentally match inside\nthe mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- and this\nvertical's domain vocabulary is an especially sharp case of that risk,\nbecause routine work-log/task text legitimately names plating baths\nand their chemistry by name (e.g. a task literally described as\n\"routine electroplating task with cyanide and chromium plating bath\"\n-- chemical identification, not a proposal to finalize a plating\noperation or clear a bath as safe). `platingcoord.governor/scope-\nexcluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as finalization ACTION\nPHRASES (\"proceed with the plating run\", \"finalize the plating\noperation\", \"declare the chemical bath safety cleared\", \"override the\nplant safety officer's judgment\"), never bare nouns, and is checked\nonly against the proposal's `:rationale` field (the advisor's own\ngenerated text), never against raw `:task` input text.\n`platingcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test driving the\ndefault mock-advisor across all four allowed ops with a task field\ncontaining exactly those bare chemical nouns, asserting none of them\never hard-trip the finalization-scope rule. Green on first run.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8122\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8122`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit,\n  not assumed, to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  6-agent batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 32 tests, 69 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/\n  counts` and independently re-verified against a brand-new fresh\n  clone of the pushed repository (not just the local working copy). No\n  mojibake in the Japanese violation-detail strings (0\n  replacement-byte instances grepped in the fresh clone).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-plating-run`/`:approve-\n  chemical-safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate path: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to\n  finalize a plating operation or a chemical-safety clearance exists\n  in the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a\n  decision whose failure mode is chemical exposure or an electrical\n  hazard incident, the capability itself must not exist in this actor\n  at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"cyanide\" \"chromium\"\n  \"electroplating\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip\n  bug class described above -- this domain's own vocabulary\n  necessarily discusses plating-bath chemistry by name to do its\n  logging/scheduling job, so a bare-noun list would self-block the\n  actor's own legitimate proposals whenever a task description\n  mentions those chemicals.\n- Naming the crew-member field `:operator-id` (matching the ISCO title\n  \"...Machine Operators\" literally): rejected -- `docs/operator-\n  guide.md` and this fleet's convention already use \"operator\" to mean\n  the deploying business/entity running the actor, so reusing the same\n  word for the individual crew member would create a confusing\n  collision; `:plater-id` (mirroring the reference's `:tanner-id`\n  pattern) keeps the two senses distinct.\n\n## Test verification\n\nFresh clone re-run immediately before writing this ADR:\n\n```text\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting platingcoord.actor-test\n\nTesting platingcoord.governor-test\n\nRan 32 tests containing 69 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n```\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :test/counts "{:total 32, :assertions 69, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Plant Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :plater-verification :facility-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :plating-operation-chemical-safety-clearance-finalization-forbidden :plant-safety-officer-override-forbidden], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8122", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122], :test/simulator :platingcoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8122 — Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Machine Operators Plant Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8122}]
